  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nHigh pressure builds into the Ohio Valley through Tuesday. Cool and \nclear conditions persist. Some patchy frost is possible tonight with \nclear skies and calm winds across the area. River valley fog is \nlikely overnight. \n\nThe first high shifts east on Tuesday night into Wednesday before \nanother area of high pressure builds in from the west during the \nsecond half of the week. Temperatures warm through Saturday while \ndry weather continues. Rain chances start to increase on Sunday into \nMonday when moisture from the Gulf States advects into the Ohio \nValley ahead of a shortwave midlevel trough.",
